# The Bricks website's route in the CMS's Caddy (ProBiz CMS docs/runbook/client-site.md). Copy to
# /srv/probiz/deploy/caddy-sites/bricks.caddy and run `docker compose restart caddy` there. It uses the
# snippets of the CMS's deploy/Caddyfile (common, website_headers, upstream). {$SITE_HOST} is the
# environment of the CMS's Caddy container: its SITE_HOST, bricks.ba.
#
# website_headers adds only `object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'`, which this site
# satisfies; it does not limit connect-src, img-src or script-src, so the browser's calls to
# https://api.bricks.ba (table ordering), next/image and the inline JSON-LD are not blocked
# (docs/runbook/deploy.md, "Content-Security-Policy").
www.{$SITE_HOST} {
	import common
	redir https://{$SITE_HOST}{uri} permanent
}

{$SITE_HOST} {
	import common
	import website_headers
	import upstream bricks-site:3000
}
